# Quick start: README.md. All variables and troubleshooting: docs/priv/deployment.md.
# Development, tests, the fake provider and several worktrees: docs/parallel-feature-foundation.md.
# Copy to `.env` (`cp .env.example .env`) and fill in the key; `.env` is ignored by Git and Docker.

# Choose one backend. The same app image supports both.
# Comfy Cloud:
COMFY_API_KEY=

# Runpod (leave COMFY_API_KEY blank):
# COMFY_BASE_URL=https://<pod-id>-8189.proxy.runpod.net
# COMFY_PROXY_TOKEN=<the pod's PROXY_TOKEN>

# Optional. The defaults suit a local `docker compose up` or `npm run dev`.

# The deployment's public HTTPS origin; share pages build their absolute Open Graph URLs from it.
# PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://photon.example

# Generations in flight at once (default 1, Comfy Cloud Standard's concurrency; 0 refuses all).
# Beyond it, new generations wait in line and the server's dispatcher starts them in order.
# IN_FLIGHT_MAX=1

# How often (ms) the dispatcher checks the line and asks Comfy about jobs in flight (default 3000).
# GENERATION_DISPATCH_MS=3000

# The header the proxy in front of the app sets to the client's address (Railway: X-Real-IP).
# Unset: the connection's own address; forwarded headers are never trusted then.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Real-IP

# The SQLite database; stored files go in `assets/` next to it (default data/app.sqlite,
# /app/data/app.sqlite in the image).
# DATABASE_PATH=data/app.sqlite

# Rate limits, per minute: uploads per client and per code, generate/retry/re-run per client
# and per code, wrong access codes per client, and wrong access codes across the instance.
# UPLOAD_RATE_LIMIT=10
# GENERATE_RATE_LIMIT=3
# LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT=10
# LOGIN_TOTAL_RATE_LIMIT=300

# 1 enables the diagnostic routes /api/debug/streams and /api/debug/heartbeat. Leave unset.
# ENABLE_DEBUG=1

# Several worktrees side by side: give each its own port, database (and with it `assets/`) and
# Compose project. Separate databases do not share one IN_FLIGHT_MAX: point real-GPU runs at
# separate targets, or coordinate them by hand.
# `npm run dev` port (default 3030); `docker compose` publishes the app on it too.
# PORT=3031
# DATABASE_PATH=data/worktree-b.sqlite
# Compose project and volume (`<name>_sqlite-data`); default: this directory's name.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=open-photon-b
# `npm run test:e2e`'s server (default http://127.0.0.1:3032, on a fresh temporary database).
# BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3033

# Development and tests only: `fake` answers every Comfy call in process with the fixtures in
# tests/fixtures/ (src/shared/server/comfy-provider.fake.ts); a built server refuses it. A target
# must still resolve and is recorded in recipes; a dead self-host port needs no key:
#   COMFY_PROVIDER=fake COMFY_API_KEY= COMFY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1
# Each submit runs COMFY_FAKE_SCENARIO (success, provider_failed or ambiguous; default success)
# unless the graph carries a [fake:<scenario>] marker; COMFY_FAKE_STEP_MS paces its events.
# COMFY_PROVIDER=fake
